-- Non-WSQ (C-prefix) courses: topics re-aligned to the course title + funding blocks pointed at the
-- correct WSQ/CASL/IBF counterpart (2026-10-05). Follows 1781 (About text).
--
-- FUNDING: every enabled C course's course_<SKU>_funding_and_grant link was resolved (incl. 301 chains)
-- and compared with the 298 enabled TGS- courses. 31 linked a generic fallback (e.g. Claude Cowork
-- Masterclass -> "Generative AI for Content Creation", AI Vibe Coding for Machine Learning -> an IBF
-- trading course) or nothing; they now link the exact/closest counterpart. Every target was curl-verified
-- 200 on its own slug (no redirect). Content-only UPDATE by identifier (updates both copies of the 2
-- duplicated identifiers; a cms/block model save would wipe cms_block_store). C16 had no block -> inserted.
--
-- TOPICS (description, LSN_DATA editor format):
--  * 21 courses whose topic list was a thin placeholder or named another course now follow their true
--    WSQ/CASL counterpart verbatim (C1259 minus the counterpart's "Mode of Assessment" entry).
--  * 4 courses with no true counterpart got a title-aligned topic list: C325 (was MS Project), C427
--    (was Codex), C1148 (was generic project management), C544 (was C976's dApp syllabus).
--  * Left alone on purpose: certification courses listing the official exam domains, and courses whose
--    list already matches the title (WSQ copies there carry typos / "Final Assesment" / an empty topic).
--  * C818 + C1143 are excluded: handled by 1782/1783 from their own courseware.
-- Topic UPDATEs are guarded by TRIM(sku) + pre-migration CHAR_LENGTH (a newer edit is never clobbered;
-- re-run = no-op). SG-only (store guard) -> no-op on MY/GH.
-- Post-deploy: flat reindex + cache flush.

SET @sg := (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM core_store WHERE store_id = 1 AND code = 'singapore');
SET @a_desc := (SELECT attribute_id FROM eav_attribute WHERE entity_type_id = 4 AND attribute_code = 'description');

